rmtfs: -D <dir>: persist the read-only (-r) RAM shadow as files

With -r every modem EFS write stays in a RAM shadow and is lost at power-off,
so the FP6 modem re-selects its platform MCFG and needs a reset on every
boot. -D keeps -r's guarantee (the partitions are only ever opened
O_RDONLY; -D without -r is refused) and additionally:
 * at open: reads the partition as before, keeps a first-capture copy in
   <dir>/original/<name>.img (0400, never replaced), and serves
   <dir>/<name>.img instead when it is valid: exact size, magic, sha256 of
   the data, and the sha256 of the same source partition contents;
 * after modem writes: saves the shadow 2 s after the last write, on CLOSE
   and at exit, as <name>.img.tmp -> fsync -> rename -> fsync(dir);
 * <dir>/RESET present: stop saving until restart.

